{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"TUIkit"}],"title":"Focus System","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusSystem"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","anchor":"Guides","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StateManagement","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ThemingGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/AppearanceAndColors","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Preferences","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/CustomViews","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/KeyboardShortcuts","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PaletteReference","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ListAndTable","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/LayoutSystem"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TUIkit provides a focus system that lets users move between interactive views (buttons, menus, text fields) using Tab, Shift+Tab, or arrow keys. The system consists of three parts:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FocusManager"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Tracks which element is focused, handles navigation"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Focusable","type":"reference"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": Protocol that views adopt to receive focus"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusState"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Lightweight state object that views use to query and request focus"}]}]}]},{"level":2,"text":"How Focus Works","anchor":"How-Focus-Works","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every frame, the ","type":"text"},{"code":"FocusManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is cleared and interactive views re-register themselves during rendering. This means focus registrations are always in sync with the current view tree: removed views are automatically unregistered.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The focus order follows the rendering order: the first focusable view rendered is first in the Tab cycle."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"The Focusable Protocol","anchor":"The-Focusable-Protocol","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Views that want to receive focus conform to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Focusable","type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public protocol Focusable: AnyObject {","    var focusID: String { get }","    var canBeFocused: Bool { get }","    func onFocusReceived()","    func onFocusLost()","    func handleKeyEvent(_ event: KeyEvent) -> Bool","}"]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"focusID"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Unique identifier for this focusable element","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"canBeFocused","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Whether focus can move to this element (default: ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onFocusReceived()"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Called when this element gains focus (default: no-op)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"onFocusLost()","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Called when this element loses focus (default: no-op)"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"handleKeyEvent(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": Handle a key event while focused; return "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" if consumed"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A default extension provides sensible defaults for ","type":"text"},{"code":"canBeFocused","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), ","type":"text"},{"code":"onFocusReceived()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"onFocusLost()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (both no-ops). Only ","type":"text"},{"code":"focusID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"handleKeyEvent(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" must be implemented.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Using FocusState","anchor":"Using-FocusState","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusState","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is the user-facing API for checking and requesting focus inside a view:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let focusState = FocusState(id: \"my-button\", focusManager: context.environment.focusManager)","","\/\/ Check if this element is currently focused","if focusState.isFocused {","    \/\/ render with focus indicator","}","","\/\/ Programmatically request focus","focusState.requestFocus()"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Built-in views like "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Button"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Menu"},{"type":"text","text":" create their own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FocusState"},{"type":"text","text":" internally: you only need it when building custom focusable views."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Navigation Keys","anchor":"Navigation-Keys","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FocusManager"},{"type":"text","text":" responds to these keys during dispatch:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Action"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tab"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Move focus to the next element","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Shift+Tab"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Move focus to the previous element","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Arrow Down \/ Right","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Move focus to the next element","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Arrow Up \/ Left"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Move focus to the previous element"}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"level":2,"text":"FocusRegistration Helper","anchor":"FocusRegistration-Helper","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Built-in interactive views use the internal ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FocusRegistration"},{"text":" helper to avoid boilerplate. It handles three tasks in one call:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist a focus ID"}]},{"type":"text","text":" via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateStorage"},{"type":"text","text":" so it remains stable across renders"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Register"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" the handler with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"FocusManager","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Query"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" whether this view currently has focus"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Custom views that implement "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Focusable"},{"type":"text","text":" typically do not need "},{"code":"FocusRegistration","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" directly. It is used by the framework’s "},{"code":"_*Core","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" views (e.g. "},{"code":"_ButtonCore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"_ListCore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Focus Indicator","anchor":"Focus-Indicator","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The visual indicator depends on the view type. Buttons and similar controls use a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"highlight background bar","type":"text"}]},{"text":" for the focused item. Text fields use ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"pulsing vertical bars"}]},{"text":" (caps) around the input area. Lists and tables use a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"highlight background","type":"text"}]},{"text":" for the focused row, with a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"pulsing accent background"}]},{"text":" when the row is both focused and selected.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Focus in the Event Loop","anchor":"Focus-in-the-Event-Loop","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Focus dispatch happens in Layer 2 of the key event pipeline (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/AppLifecycle","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"):"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A key event arrives from stdin"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Layer 1 (status bar) gets first chance to handle it","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Layer 2: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyEventDispatcher"},{"type":"text","text":" dispatches to the focused view’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"handleKeyEvent(_:)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If not consumed, navigation keys (Tab, arrows) are handled by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FocusManager"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Layer 3 (default bindings) handles quit, theme cycling, etc.","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tuikit\/focussystem"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Navigate between interactive elements using the keyboard."}],"references":{"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/FocusState":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"FocusState"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"FocusState","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tracks focus state for a specific element."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusState","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/focusstate","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FocusState"}]},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/Menu":{"title":"Menu","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Menu"}],"identifier":"do